{"id": "5ae8b5de-8487-4697-a871-eef7b438baf1", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check Bedrock's CloudWatch metrics for the last 14 days in us-east-1. I'm looking at cache reads, cache writes, and regular input tokens for each model, so I can work out your cache hit rate and whether caching is saving you money.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_ehIqTEGkTLQgzxM6ndGQ5A", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-cache-roi", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether Amazon Bedrock prompt caching is paying off for this account over the last 14 days in us-east-1.",
  "context": "User asks 'Is prompt caching paying off for us?'. Assume Amazon Bedrock prompt caching (AWS/Bedrock CloudWatch namespace). Read-only analysis only; do not make any mutating calls. Agent space account is 123456789012 (use list_associations to find other associated accounts and check those too if relevant).",
  "resources": ["CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock, region us-east-1", "Metrics: InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, CacheReadInputTokenCount, CacheWriteInputTokenCount, Invocations, InvocationLatency (per ModelId dimension)"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-09T21:00:00Z/2026-11-23T21:00:00Z",
  "criteria": "1) Use list_metrics to discover which ModelIds (and inference profile IDs) emit cache metrics, and which models have significant traffic but zero cache usage. 2) Per model and overall, compute totals over 14 days (use daily period sums): CacheReadInputTokenCount, CacheWriteInputTokenCount, InputTokenCount (note: InputTokenCount excludes cached tokens - verify via docs with verify_aws_claim if unsure), and the cache hit rate = cacheRead / (cacheRead + cacheWrite + input). 3) Estimate net cost impact using current published Bedrock on-demand pricing for each model (verify pricing via verify_aws_claim or docs; typically cache reads are ~10% of base input price and cache writes are ~125% of base input price for Anthropic models; state clearly any assumption and if pricing is uncertain). Compare cost with caching vs hypothetical cost without caching (all tokens at base input price). 4) Show daily trend of hit rate to see whether it's improving/degrading, and flag models where write tokens greatly exceed read tokens (caching losing money / break-even requires roughly reads >= ~0.3x writes per write for 5-minute TTL). 5) Note if no cache metrics exist at all. Return a concise summary with a per-model table (numbers), overall verdict, and any caveats. Shallow pass; suggest deeper follow-ups."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Analyze Bedrock prompt caching metrics in us-east-1 for 14 days"}], "created_at": null}

